Preserve the selected Bazel Zig target and its glibc floor for all code.

cc-rs probes compiler identity with a standalone CC --version. Zig 0.14
main.zig punts no-input commands directly to clangMain with the original
arguments. Clang cannot parse the wrapper's Zig-only glibc suffix in
-target aarch64-linux-gnu.2.17 and reports an invalid
aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu.2.17 triple. A standalone version query needs no
target; do not add one. Every preprocessing, compile and link invocation
still gets the authoritative Zig target, including its glibc 2.17 floor.

rustc also passes -Wl,-O1 for optimized Linux links. Zig 0.14's main.zig
only records this option to emit "ignoring deprecated linker optimization
setting '1'"; it never affects the link. Omit that exact no-op, without
suppressing diagnostics or changing C/C++ optimization flags.

Applied after hermetic_cc_toolchain-drop-cortex-a53-link-arg.patch.

diff --git a/toolchain/zig-wrapper.zig b/toolchain/zig-wrapper.zig
--- a/toolchain/zig-wrapper.zig
+++ b/toolchain/zig-wrapper.zig
@@ -261,7 +261,10 @@
     while (argv_it.next()) |arg| {
+        // Zig ignores this deprecated rustc linker setting already.
+        if (run_mode == RunMode.cc and mem.eql(u8, arg, "-Wl,-O1"))
+            continue;
         // rustc adds this on aarch64 linux (rust-lang/rust#155453); zig cc
         // rejects both spellings.
         if (run_mode == RunMode.cc and (mem.eql(u8, arg, "-Wl,--fix-cortex-a53-843419") or mem.eql(u8, arg, "-mfix-cortex-a53-843419")))
             continue;
         try args.append(arena, arg);
     }
@@ -301,10 +304,14 @@
     // Add -target as the last parameter. The wrapper should overwrite
     // the target specified by other tools calling the wrapper.
     // Some tools might pass LLVM target triple, which are rejected by zig.
     // https://github.com/uber/hermetic_cc_toolchain/issues/222
-    if (run_mode == RunMode.cc) {
+    // Zig punts a standalone --version query directly to Clang, which
+    // rejects Zig's glibc suffix. No code is built by this version query;
+    // keep it target-independent and retain the pinned target for all code.
+    const version_query = args.items.len == 3 and mem.eql(u8, args.items[2], "--version");
+    if (run_mode == RunMode.cc and !version_query) {
         try args.appendSlice(arena, &[_][]const u8{
             "-target",
             run_mode.cc,
         });
     }
